      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your discovery is a game-changer, and you're right to be cautious. To establish credibility, consider reaching out to reputable comic book historians, lawyers, or experts in intellectual property law who can help you verify the authenticity and significance of the documents. A well-documented, expert-backed claim is more likely to resonate with Warner Bros. than a solo, unverified assertion. You may also want to start by drafting a clear, concise, and respectful letter outlining your findings and proposed next steps, which you can then use as a foundation for negotiations.",
